y. It failed because git isn't available (no .git). That's an environment limitation, not my change. The spec validate passed. Let me note this.\n\nLet me also try `node harness/src/cli.mjs explain` to see selected steps.\n\nActually validate passed which is the key gate. The dry-run requires git for changed-file detection. Since the workspace has no git repo, that check can't run. I'll report it honestly.\n\nLet me now finalize. I should double-check the harness validate with the actual `--spec` and also verify ownership: since no git, changedFiles empty, so ownership vacuously passes.\n\nLet me also run the lifecycle check scoped: my spec has lifecycleStatus, no new failures.\n\nLet me clean up temp files.\n\nLet me verify final deliverables exist and re-confirm the module is byte-identical to reference.\n\nOne more: should I add the `contextPressureRecoveryDigest` helper? The reference doesn't have it; I reverted to exact bytes so it's gone. Fine — exact match is safest.\n\nLet me do a final listing."}}
